# Commit Conventions

- Use imperative mood: “Add asset soft-delete service”, not “Added” / “Adds”.
- Subject ≈ 72 characters; optional body for *why* and notable tradeoffs.
- One concern per commit (feature, fix, refactor, test, chore).
- Reference module when useful: `Asset: block folder delete when non-empty`.
- Do not commit `.env`, secrets, `node_modules`, `vendor`, or generated Wayfinder `actions`/`routes`.
- Do not use `--no-verify` to skip Husky unless explicitly requested.

Examples:

```
Add FolderService depth validation on create

Enforce max depth of 2 in the service layer so Form Requests stay
focused on input shape.
```

```
Fix API error envelope for FolderNotEmptyException
```
